systemd automatically enables the service getty@tty1.service to start a virtual
console on the (pseudo) tty1 at boot. Consoles on ttys up to tty6 will be
created on demand when you switch to them using Ctrl+Alt+{F1-F6}.

To override the default options for the getty@tty1.service, we will create a
dropin file at %1.
We will override the ExecStart option to override the parameters passed to
agetty, Arch Linux's default getty provider. You might notice the peculiar line
ExecStart=
in the file. This is needed to clear out the existing value of the ExecStart
option. This pattern is commonly used in systemd drop-in files for overwriting
existing options that allow multiple declarations.

On the actual replacement line, we will be passing the following parameters:
    - skip-login: skips prompting for a login name, effectively facilitating
        automatic log in
    - nonewline: removes the newline before the welcome message
    - noissue: removes the welcome message itself
    - autologin %2: specifies %2 as the user for the automatic log in
    - noreset: keeps the virtual console's control modes as is
    - noclear: doesn't clear the screen before prompting (or rather not
        prompting) for a user

The "${TERM}" passed as an argument refers to the virtual console.

